From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: Control, ContentControl, UserControl, Page

Applications derive their pages and user controls from Page and UserControl; NanaZip stopped at Windows.UI.Xaml.Controls.Page. Control (composable) with its properties (Foreground, FontSize, FontFamily, FontWeight, FontStyle, Padding, Background, BorderBrush, BorderThickness, CornerRadius, content alignments, IsEnabled, IsTabStop, TabIndex, Template, DefaultStyleKey ...), its Background and border drawn, Padding and BorderThickness around its content, and its text properties passed down to the TextBlocks inside it (value inheritance); ContentControl whose Content is shown -- an element as its child, a string as text; UserControl and Page with an element Content; Page's Frame and app bars kept; the overridable input methods answer for themselves. Templates and styles come later. Interface identity per windows-rs 0.30.0 (MIT OR Apache-2.0), overridable methods' names per the public API documentation; the implementation is ours. Behind the XAML switch of 6131.
---
